arrow pointing at the region, such as a button. Fields: start, end, target or x/y/width/height.\n- circle (Overlays): A ring around the region. Fields: start, end, target or x/y/width/height.\n- progress (Overlays): A thin bar that fills from start to end. position: top or bottom. Fields: start, end, position.\n- speed (Timing): Plays that stretch faster or slower: rate 0.5 to 2, never 1. The voice keeps its pitch. Fields: start, end, rate.\n- freeze (Timing): Holds the picture at start until end (at most 5 s) while the voice goes on. Fields: start, end.\n- jumpCut (Timing): Cuts those words out. Fields: startWord, endWord.\n- zoom (Timing): A punch-in for that stretch: scale 1.05 to 1.35. Fields: start, end, scale.\n- correction (Words): Fixes one misheard word: text is the right spelling. Fields: startWord, text.\n- rewrite (Words): Re-records those words in the creator's own voice saying text. This one is paid; the creator approves it with one click. Fields: startWord, endWord, text.\n- translate (Words): Shows the captions of those words in another language: language is a code such as es or de, text the translation. Fields: startWord, endWord, language, text.\n- music (Sound): Changes the clip's background music: text describes the mood. Generated music is paid; the creator approves it with one click. Fields: text.\n- duck (Sound): Lowers the background music under the voice. Fields: start, end.\n- sound (Sound): A short sound effect at start: sound is whoosh, pop or ding. Fields: start, sound.\n\nReturn the operations."
